-       import htmlDoms.whatwg.*
+       import htmlDoms.whatwg.*

-       Div(P("Hello"))
+       Div(P("Hello"))

=       Div(P("Hello"))
-       ```
+       ```

-       `Whatwg` is the HTML Living Standard, what "HTML" means today, and suits almost every
-       use; `Html4Transitional` is HTML 4.01 Transitional, for a program which must emit or
-       read that dialect's presentational tags and attributes. Reading (`read[Html]`,
-       `load[Html]`) needs a `Dom` in scope; rendering with `show` always uses the WHATWG one,
-       and a streamed `Document[Html]` uses the DOM recorded in its `Html.Provenance`.
+       `Whatwg` é o HTML Living Standard, o que “HTML” significa hoje, e serve para quase todo
+       uso; `Html4Transitional` é o HTML 4.01 Transitional, para um programa que precisa emitir
+       ou ler as tags e os atributos de apresentação desse dialeto. A leitura (`read[Html]`,
+       `load[Html]`) requer um `Dom` no escopo; a renderização com `show` sempre usa o WHATWG, e
+       um `Document[Html]` transmitido usa o DOM registrado no seu `Html.Provenance`.

=       and a streamed `Document[Html]` uses the DOM recorded in its `Html.Provenance`.
